   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT authorizing William Bianco and Eric Lipinsky to file for retroactive membership in the optional 20 year retirement plan of the New York state and local police and fire retirement system pursuant to section 384-d of the retirement and social security law",
    "basePrintNo": "S6861",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6861-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Retirement",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6861\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act authorizing William Bianco and Eric Lipinsky to file for\nretroactive membership in the optional 20 year retirement plan of the\nNew York state and local police and fire retirement system pursuant to\nsection 384-d of the retirement and social security law\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nTo allow William Bianco and Eric Lipinsky to file for retroactive\nmembership in the Town of Riverhead's optional 20 year retirement plan\nof the New York state and local police and fire retirement system.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection 1. Provides that the Town of Riverhead is authorized to allow\nWilliam Bianco and Eric Lipinsky to timely file applications to\nparticipate in the town's option retirement plan.\nSection 2. Provides that all past service costs will be borne by the\nTown of Riverhead.\nSection 3. Provides that the act shall take effect immediately.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe Town of Riverhead adopted an optional 20 year retirement plan\npursuant to section 384-d and e of the retirement and social law which\nallowed a limited time period for its officers to opt into the plan.\nThe Town, by resolution, has determined that the officers, for no\nreasons ascribable to their intentional negligence, did not opt into\nthe plan and supports legislation which will allow them to make timely\napplications.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n$11,000 past service cost to be paid by the Town of Riverhead with\nongoing costs of annual contributions of $6,900.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
